Provides examples and tutorials for common CloudWatch alarm uses cases.

- [Create a billing alarm](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/monitor_estimated_charges_with_cloudwatch.md): Walks through how to monitor your estimated charges using CloudWatch.
- [Create a CPU usage alarm](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/US_AlarmAtThresholdEC2.md): Walks through how to create an CloudWatch alarm that sends a notification based on CPU usage.
- [Create a load balancer latency alarm](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/US_AlarmAtThresholdELB.md): Walks through how to create a load balancer alarm based on excess latency.
- [Create a storage throughput alarm](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/US_AlarmAtThresholdEBS.md): Walks through how to create a storage throughput alarm based on Amazon EBS that exceeds 100-MB throughput.
- [Create an alarm on Performance Insights counter metrics from an AWS database](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_alarm_database_performance_insights.md): Walks through how to create an alarm based on Performance Insights metrics that you retrieve from Amazon RDS or Amazon DocumentDB.
- [Create a Log Alarm on errors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/US_LogAlarmErrorPattern.md): Walks through how to create a Log Alarm that detects error patterns in log data.
- [Create a Log Alarm on latency](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/US_LogAlarmLatencyByEndpoint.md): Walks through how to create a multi-contributor Log Alarm that monitors latency across API endpoints.


## [Telemetry discovery and enablement](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/telemetry-config-cloudwatch.md)

- [What is telemetry discovery and enablement?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/telemetry-config-what-is.md): CloudWatch telemetry configuration gives you two core capabilities:

### [Setting up telemetry configuration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/telemetry-config-turn-on.md)

Learn how to enable and configure telemetry for your AWS account or organization using the CloudWatch console to discover resources and set up telemetry collection.

- [Enable telemetry configuration for your organization](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/telemetry-config-organization.md): To turn on telemetry configuration for your organization, you must use a AWS Organization management account or a delegated administrator account.
- [Discovering resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/telemetry-config-view-resources.md): The telemetry configuration experience displays AWS resources in two places: as an overview on the Ingestion – Data sources and in detail on the Discovered resources page.
- [Telemetry enablement rules](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/telemetry-config-rules.md): Learn how to create and manage telemetry rules to standardize telemetry collection across your AWS resources.
- [Troubleshooting telemetry configuration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/telemetry-config-troubleshoot.md): Common issues and solutions when working with telemetry configuration.
- [Disabling telemetry configuration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/telemetry-config-turn-off.md): When you no longer need telemetry configuration, you can turn it off.


## [Infrastructure monitoring](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch-Insights-Sections.md)

### [Container Insights](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ContainerInsights.md)

How to use Container Insights to collect metrics and logs from your containers.

### [Amazon EKS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/deploy-container-insights-EKS.md)

Set up and use CloudWatch Container Insights on Amazon EKS clusters.

### [OTel Container Insights (Recommended)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel.md)

Use OTel Container Insights to collect metrics and logs from Amazon EKS clusters with a simplified OpenTelemetry-based deployment.

- [Quick start: OTel Container Insights on Amazon EKS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel-quickstart.md): Enable OTel Container Insights on an existing Amazon EKS cluster by using the AWS Management Console or the AWS CLI.
- [Enable OTel Container Insights from the console](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel-console.md): Enable OTel Container Insights on an existing Amazon EKS cluster by using the AWS Management Console with a minimal-click workflow.
- [Deploy OTel Container Insights with Helm](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel-helm.md): Deploy OTel Container Insights on Amazon EKS by using the Amazon CloudWatch Observability Helm chart with the OpenTelemetry filelog receiver for log collection.
- [Deploy OTel Container Insights with CloudFormation](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel-cfn.md): Deploy OTel Container Insights on Amazon EKS as infrastructure as code by using a CloudFormation template.
- [Sending logs to Amazon CloudWatch](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel-logs.md): Collect and send container logs to CloudWatch Logs by using the OTel Container Insights log pipeline on Amazon EKS.
- [Install the CloudWatch agent with the Amazon CloudWatch Observability EKS add-on or the Helm chart](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/install-CloudWatch-Observability-EKS-addon.md): Explains how to install the CloudWatch agent by installing the CloudWatch Observability EKS add-on.
- [Advanced configuration for OTel Container Insights on Amazon EKS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel-advanced.md): Configure custom metrics, log filters, multi-account collection, custom dimensions, and resource tuning for OTel Container Insights on Amazon EKS.

### [Solutions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel-solutions.md)

With Solutions, you can get pre-built observability for third-party Kubernetes tools that run on your Amazon EKS clusters.

- [Karpenter metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel-karpenter.md): Collect Karpenter node autoscaler metrics through OTel Container Insights to gain visibility into node provisioning, scaling performance, and resource utilization on Amazon EKS.
- [KEDA metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/container-insights-eks-otel-keda.md): Collect KEDA event-driven autoscaling metrics through OTel Container Insights to gain visibility into ScaledObject status, scaler health, and scale loop performance on Amazon EKS.

