- [Using the PutLogEvents API to send manually-created embedded metric format logs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Embedded_Metric_Format_Generation_PutLogEvents.md): Explains how to generate embedded metric format logs by using the PutLogEvents API.
- [Using the CloudWatch agent to send embedded metric format logs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Embedded_Metric_Format_Generation_CloudWatch_Agent.md): Explains how to generate embedded metric format logs by using the CloudWatch agent.
- [Using the embedded metric format with AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Embedded_Metric_Format_OpenTelemetry.md): Explains how to use embedded metric format with the AWS Distro for OpenTelemetry.
- [Viewing your metrics and logs in the console](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Embedded_Metric_Format_View.md): Explains how to view the metrics and logs from embedded metric format logs.
- [Setting alarms on metrics created with the embedded metric format](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/CloudWatch_Embedded_Metric_Format_Alarms.md): Explains important details about setting alarms on metrics that were created using CloudWatch embedded metric format.

### [CloudWatch pipelines](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/cloudwatch-pipelines.md)

CloudWatch pipelines is a managed data pipeline solution that streamlines the collection, filtering, and routing of telemetry and security data from AWS services and third-party sources.

- [Creating pipelines](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/Creating-pipelines.md): Use the pipeline configuration wizard to create data processing pipelines through a guided process that configures sources, processors, and destinations.
- [Managing pipelines](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/managing-pipelines.md): Monitor pipeline health, view processing metrics, and manage pipeline lifecycle through the Pipelines dashboard.

### [Supported data sources for CloudWatch](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/data-sources.md)

CloudWatch supports a broad range of data sources including AWS services, third-party security and identity platforms, and custom log sources.

- [CloudWatch Metrics (OTel)](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/metrics-pipeline-selection-criteria.md): Define which OpenTelemetry metrics enter a metrics pipeline using OTTL path expressions.

### [Third-party data sources integration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/third-party-integration-setup.md)

Connect external security tools, identity providers, and monitoring platforms to CloudWatch pipelines for centralized log analysis.

