### [Custom log data from CloudWatch Logs or an Amazon S3 bucket](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/ingestion-custom-data-sources.md)

Create CloudWatch pipelines pipelines for custom application logs stored in CloudWatch Logs or Amazon S3 buckets.

- [Configuring Custom S3 Bucket Sources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/configuring-custom-s3-bucket-sources.md): With CloudWatch pipelines, you can process arbitrary logs stored in S3 buckets.
- [AWS service logs from CloudWatch Logs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/aws-service-logs-from-cwl.md): Configure CloudWatch Logs from an AWS service as a data source

### [Processors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/pipeline-processors.md)

Configure data transformation and enrichment for your pipeline.

- [Parser processors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/parser-processors.md): Parser processors convert raw or semi-structured log data into structured formats.
- [Transformation processors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/transformation-processors.md): Transformation processors modify the structure of log events by adding, copying, moving, or removing fields.
- [String manipulation processors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/string-processors.md): String processors modify text values within log events through operations like case conversion, trimming, and pattern matching.
- [Filter processors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/filter-processors.md): Filter processors let you selectively remove log entries from the pipeline based on conditions you define.
- [Common processor use cases](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/processor-examples.md): Here are common scenarios and example configurations for combining processors.
- [Processor compatibility and restrictions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/processor-compatibility.md)
- [Metrics processors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/metrics-pipeline-processors.md): Transform and enrich OpenTelemetry metrics as they flow through a metrics pipeline.
- [Expression syntax for conditional processing](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/conditional-processing.md): Expression syntax reference for CloudWatch pipelines conditional processing.
- [Sinks](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/pipeline-sinks.md): Configure destinations for processed pipeline data.
- [CloudWatch pipelines IAM policies and permissions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/pipeline-iam-reference.md): This section provides IAM requirements for CloudWatch pipelines.
- [Extensions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/pipeline-extensions.md): Configure additional pipeline functionality.
- [Monitoring pipelines](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/pipelines-metrics.md): Monitor your CloudWatch pipelines' health, performance, and data flow using Amazon CloudWatch metrics in the AWS/Observability Admin namespace.
- [Troubleshooting](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/troubleshooting.md): Common issues and solutions for CloudWatch pipelines configuration, data processing, and performance optimization.

### [Managed Prometheus collectors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/managed-prometheus-collectors.md)

Use fully managed, agentless collectors to automatically discover and scrape Prometheus-compatible metrics from your AWS resources and send them to CloudWatch.

- [Integrate Amazon MSK](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/managed-prometheus-collectors-msk-setup.md): Use a Amazon CloudWatch managed Prometheus collector to automatically discover and collect Prometheus metrics from your Amazon MSK clusters and deliver them to CloudWatch.
- [Integrate Amazon OpenSearch Service](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/managed-prometheus-collectors-opensearch-setup.md): Use a Amazon CloudWatch managed Prometheus collector to automatically collect Prometheus-compatible metrics from your Amazon OpenSearch Service domains and deliver them to CloudWatch.
- [Integrate Amazon EKS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/managed-prometheus-collectors-eks-setup.md): Use a Amazon CloudWatch managed Prometheus collector to automatically discover and collect Prometheus metrics from your Amazon EKS clusters and deliver them to CloudWatch.
- [VPC-connected managed collector](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/managed-prometheus-collectors-vpc-setup.md): Use a VPC-connected managed collector to scrape Prometheus-compatible metrics from any resource reachable within your VPC.
- [Scraper configuration](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/managed-prometheus-collectors-scraper-configuration.md): Configure the scraper using Prometheus-compatible YAML to define scrape targets, intervals, and relabeling rules.
- [Monitor collectors](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/monitoring/managed-prometheus-collectors-monitor.md): Monitor the health and status of your managed Prometheus collectors using vended logs, and manage scrapers with the AWS CLI.


